  "schema": 1,
  "record": "Milestone A acceptance measurement, run 2026-09-18",
  "why": "The measurement used to select its before cohort with a directory glob over a session scratchpad, and to drop three rounds by observing that they classified to zero output. A scratchpad is temporary, and a date glob over the session store would mix the two cohorts, because the dates these rollouts fall on hold 108 sessions: fourteen before rollouts, four after rollouts, and ninety outside both cohorts. This file states the cohort instead: every input by session stem and SHA-256, and which of them the published table counts.",
  "acquisition": "Each stem names a Codex rollout. By default the measurement resolves them under ~/.codex/sessions, which is per-machine application storage that can be archived or pruned. Keep a copy outside it and pass --corpus-dir <path>, or set ACCEPTANCE_CORPUS_DIR, to measure from the frozen copy. The raw rollouts total 68,114,296 bytes (about 68 MB or 65 MiB) for the before cohort and are not committed. Resolution matches <stem>*.jsonl recursively; a missing, ambiguous, or hash-mismatched input fails the run.",
  "corpus_root_default": "~/.codex/sessions",
